WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We talked about it
briefly backstage,

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.369 line:92%
but the first film I saw you in

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:03.937
was a wonderful Australian crime
film, "Animal Kingdom."

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:06.806
-Indeed, the series
of the same name is based on it.

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:10.076 size:88% position:44%
-Yeah, and you were very
villainous in that role.

00:00:10.076 --> 00:00:13.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, he's not a nice guy.
-He's not a nice guy.

00:00:13.013 --> 00:00:13.680 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-He's not a nice guy.

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.682
His name is Pope, so I guess...
-Yeah.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:18.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Pope, King -- yeah.
-Yeah, exactly.

00:00:18.385 --> 00:00:20.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
No gray area on him.
Very much --

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nobody walked out
of that film being like,

00:00:21.554 --> 00:00:24.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I liked him the most."
-Some did.

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:25.692 line:92%
But, you know, Australians,

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.460 align:start size:94% position:6%
they have peculiar sense
of this stuff.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:30.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you still get recognized
from that film?

00:00:30.563 --> 00:00:31.131 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah. A bit.

00:00:31.131 --> 00:00:33.867 size:81% position:41%
I mean, but they don't
tend to come up to me.

00:00:33.867 --> 00:00:35.301
-Yeah.
-So that one it's sort of like,

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:37.537 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Oh, yeah,
they saw 'Animal Kingdom,'"

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:39.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause they just
sort of go away.

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:43.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know more if it's
"Bloodline" or "Star Wars."

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:46.246
-And I want to -- It's very nice
to see you in this role,

00:00:46.246 --> 00:00:48.581
because you play a nice person.
-Yes.

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:50.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was really lovely
to see you play a nice person.

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:51.684 size:78% position:39%
-Thank you very much.
-And you actually --

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because that was --
For people that don't know,

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:55.488 size:78% position:39%
that was Gary Oldman
as Winston Churchill.

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:56.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
Unrecognizable.
-That is Gary Oldman.

00:00:56.923 --> 00:01:00.260 size:84% position:42%
-You look a fair amount
like King George here.

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's not bad.
-Yeah. I think, uh...

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:05.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think, you know, Joe --
You know, Joe --

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:06.666 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's why he gave me the job.
-Yeah.

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:08.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You look like him.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:09.235 line:92%
-Yeah, he was like, look,

00:01:09.235 --> 00:01:11.471 size:84% position:42%
"I'm wasting my entire
makeup budget on Gary."

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:12.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yep.
-I need some --

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:13.640 line:92%
Everybody else has to look

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.408 align:start size:94% position:6%
exactly like
who they're playing.

00:01:15.408 --> 00:01:17.243 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yep. That's it.

00:01:17.243 --> 00:01:19.245 line:92%
-Famously, obviously, this is --

00:01:19.245 --> 00:01:20.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're playing someone
who had a lisp.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:22.449
You had to use a dialect coach.
-Yep.

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:23.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How was that?
Was that intense?

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah,
it's pretty full on.

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:28.421 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Yeah, I mean, the --

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:31.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
It starts to happen.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.558 --> 00:01:33.693
-Even thinking --
Even saying dialect coach now...

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:36.096 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And once you start
to get close to them,

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:38.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
they start to invade you
at various times.

00:01:38.832 --> 00:01:40.800 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, yeah.
It was a lot of work.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:45.171
"The King's Speech" is the same
character a little earlier on.

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:47.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
A little bit of a worse,
you know, stutter.

00:01:47.807 --> 00:01:48.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Wow.
So you had to go back.

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:49.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
You had to step back
from even that.

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:53.780
-I had to go forward from that,
yes, to step back from that.

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:55.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, gotcha.
-Yeah.

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:58.118
-One of the great things
about the new "Star Wars" films,

00:01:58.118 --> 00:02:00.887
so many people were fans
and happy to see them back.

00:02:00.887 --> 00:02:03.623
I'm always happy to hear that
the actors who are lucky enough

00:02:03.623 --> 00:02:04.491 line:92%
to be in those films were fans.

00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:05.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were a fan of "Star Wars"?
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:07.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, I mean,
the first one comes out,

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:09.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm in the cinema,
I'm 8 years old,

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:13.500
and then, "BVVVV!"
the ship comes overhead, I'm in.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:14.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's great.
-Yeah.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:17.737
-And so was there a moment
on set that you realized,

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:20.807
"Oh, I'm in a 'Star Wars' movie
right now"?

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:21.541 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah, once --

00:02:21.541 --> 00:02:23.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
So you do the rehearsals,
and this and that,

00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:25.478 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you know
you're gonna be in it,

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:26.179 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
but, you know --

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:27.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
For those of you
that don't know,

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:29.582
I kind of built the Death Star.
-Yeah.

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:31.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-And, um, so...

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:33.286
-And that's great,
because, really, when you think,

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:35.321 size:84% position:42%
King George didn't do
anything close to that.

00:02:35.321 --> 00:02:37.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, well, you know.
-[ Laughing ]

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:39.159 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I mean, yeah.

00:02:39.159 --> 00:02:41.828
Different, but when you have
those stormtroopers there,

00:02:41.828 --> 00:02:43.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
yeah, you know you're in
a "Star Wars" movie.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.665 size:84% position:42%
-That's really great,
and you had a lot of --

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:48.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
You had just
teams of stormtroopers

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:49.802 size:88% position:44% line:92%
behind you in that film.

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:50.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I did.
I did, indeed.

00:02:50.637 --> 00:02:53.406
-Yeah, congratulations on that.
-Thank you very much.

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:56.242
-First time you saw Darth Vader,
how was that?

00:02:56.242 --> 00:03:00.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was -- You know, it was
personal, I guess.

00:03:00.113 --> 00:03:00.713 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.713 --> 00:03:02.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you keep -- No,
I genuinely want to ask this.

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:05.952
Did you keep your cool the first
time you saw Darth Vader on set?

00:03:05.952 --> 00:03:07.220 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
No, not at all.

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I mean, not at all.

00:03:08.755 --> 00:03:10.790 align:start size:94% position:6%
For a start, he's enormous.
-Yeah.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.126
-He's got
a really bad breathing problem.

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:14.394 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, like --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.394 --> 00:03:16.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
You think George
has got problems speaking?

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:19.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it's hard for Darth.
-Yeah.

00:03:19.232 --> 00:03:21.034 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But, you know,
I mean you stay there,

00:03:21.034 --> 00:03:23.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
you listen, and, in fact,
there kind of are

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:25.905
similarities between King George
and Darth in that way.

00:03:25.905 --> 00:03:28.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And does Darth show up
for rehearsal and everything?

00:03:28.908 --> 00:03:30.710 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, no, never.
No, no, no.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:31.277 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Darth, I mean --

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:33.279 size:88% position:44%
There's a stand-in guy
that does Darth's stuff.

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:33.813 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay, gotcha.

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.481
-And then you'd be waiting
around, and it'd be like,

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:37.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Okay,
Darth's gonna be here soon."

00:03:37.617 --> 00:03:39.485
It's like,
"Darth's going to be here soon,"

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:41.888 size:75% position:38%
and then you hear --
[ Breathing loudly ]

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:44.290
-Is he ever apologetic
about keeping everyone waiting?

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:46.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Never apologizes.
Never explains.

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:48.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
That seems to be
one of his things.

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:49.829 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't know.
It's just a shame.

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:51.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's that kind of guy,
but, look...

00:03:51.097 --> 00:03:52.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a shame
he doesn't try harder.

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:55.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
the work is wonderful though,
so, you know, whatever.

00:03:55.902 --> 00:03:57.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have heard --
We share something else.

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
We are both comic-book fans.
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:59.539 --> 00:04:02.575
-Is that something you were
a fan of your whole life?

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:03.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Yes and no.

00:04:03.810 --> 00:04:05.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean,
I'm a mild comic-book fan.

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:07.914
I wouldn't want to go toe-to-toe
with a serious one.

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:08.348 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:10.783
-I'm talking about
the Kirby kind of "X-Men" years.

00:04:10.783 --> 00:04:13.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm talking McFarlane's --
-Seth McFarlane, yeah.

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:17.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Spider-Man" stuff?
-Exactly, and later, "Spawn."

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:17.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, great.
-Yeah.

00:04:17.991 --> 00:04:19.692 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There we go.
We match up very well on that.

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:21.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There you go.
-And you mentioned --

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:22.528 line:92%
You mentioned "Bloodline,"

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:23.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
getting recognized more
for "Bloodline."

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:26.199 line:92%
Do you find the TV work you do

00:04:26.199 --> 00:04:28.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
you get recognized
more for than your --

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:29.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Okay.

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:31.704
-Because people spend more time
with you on TV.

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:34.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm in the lounge room,
as it were.

00:04:34.507 --> 00:04:35.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-You know, whereas

00:04:35.375 --> 00:04:37.477
they don't expect
to see someone from "Star Wars"

00:04:37.477 --> 00:04:40.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
walking down the street.
You know what I mean?

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:42.615
-That's true.
-There's a bit of a disconnect.

00:04:42.615 --> 00:04:44.350 line:92%
-Yeah, because when you think --

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
You look more like
your character in "Bloodline"

00:04:46.386 --> 00:04:49.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
in real life than you do
in your "Star Wars" character.

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:51.491 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-I think?

00:04:51.491 --> 00:04:53.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:56.029
I never thought of it that way,
that you'd be very surprised

00:04:56.029 --> 00:04:56.829 line:92%
to see someone, and you're like,

00:04:56.829 --> 00:04:57.997 align:start size:94% position:6%
"When was last time
I saw that guy?"

00:04:57.997 --> 00:04:59.499 align:start size:94% position:6%
You'd be like,
"Oh, the Death Star."

00:04:59.499 --> 00:05:00.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:02.135 size:75% position:38%
-It would definitely
take you a minute.

00:05:02.135 --> 00:05:04.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it does.
It takes them a minute, yeah.

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:06.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, congratulations
on the film.

00:05:06.673 --> 00:05:07.206 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you.

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:08.808
-And in general,
just such a delight to meet you.

00:05:08.808 --> 00:05:10.843 line:92%
Thanks so much for being here.

